# HARP reference server: manual flow.
# Run the server first (pnpm dev), then send these top to bottom.
# Compatible with the VS Code REST Client extension.

@base = http://localhost:4000

### 1. Discover the manifest
GET {{base}}/auth.md

### 2. Read Protected Resource Metadata
GET {{base}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

### 3. Read authorization-server metadata (agent_auth block)
GET {{base}}/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

### 4. DEV: mint a test ID-JAG
# Copy "assertion" from the response into the requests below.
POST {{base}}/dev/mint-id-jag
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sub": "user_madison", "org_id": "org_acme", "email_verified": true }

### 5. Register with the ID-JAG (returns a base token, no PHI scopes yet)
POST {{base}}/agent/identity
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "identity_assertion", "assertion": "PASTE_ASSERTION" }

### 6. Try eligibility with a PHI scope before BAA: expect 403 baa_required
POST {{base}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grant_type": "urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer", "assertion": "PASTE_ASSERTION", "scope": "rcm.eligibility:read" }

### 7. Accept the BAA for the org
POST {{base}}/agent/baa/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{ "org_id": "org_acme", "baa_version_hash": "sha256:demo-baa-v1", "accepted_by": "ric@goneomics.com", "signature": "demo-sig" }

### 8. Exchange again, now with BAA accepted: returns a PHI-scoped token
POST {{base}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grant_type": "urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer", "assertion": "PASTE_ASSERTION", "scope": "rcm.eligibility:read" }

### 9. Call the protected resource with the PHI-scoped token
GET {{base}}/eligibility?member=demo-member
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN
x-harp-purpose-of-use: PAYMENT

### 10. Verify the receipt returned in step 9
POST {{base}}/agent/receipt/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "receipt": PASTE_RECEIPT_OBJECT }
